#. ARCH_OS_USERNAME: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Username"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_USERNAME: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The account you log in with."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_USERNAME: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Identity"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_USERNAME: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Lowercase letters, digits, hyphens and underscores only, up to 32 characters. It cannot start with a digit."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_PASSWORD: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Password"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_PASSWORD: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "For your account and, with disk encryption, to unlock the disk at boot unless it has a password of its own. Asked right before the installation and never written to a file."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_HOSTNAME: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Hostname"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_HOSTNAME: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The name this machine has on the network."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_HOSTNAME: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Lowercase letters, digits and hyphens only, up to 63 characters. It cannot start or end with a hyphen."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_LOCALE_LANG: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Language and region"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_LOCALE_LANG: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The system language and the format of dates, numbers and currency, such as de_DE. On auto the keyboard, console font and time zone follow it. English is always installed as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_LOCALE_LANG: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Region"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_VCONSOLE_KEYMAP: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Console keyboard"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_VCONSOLE_KEYMAP: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The keyboard you are typing on right now, loaded at once and used on the text console. auto follows the system language."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_VCONSOLE_FONT: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Console font"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_VCONSOLE_FONT: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The font of the text console. auto picks one for the language; a larger one helps on a high-resolution screen."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_TIMEZONE: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Time zone"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_TIMEZONE: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Where this machine is, so the clock is right. Opens on the zone of the chosen country."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_REFLECTOR_COUNTRY: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Mirror country"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_REFLECTOR_COUNTRY: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Where packages are downloaded from. auto follows the time zone, none ranks every mirror worldwide."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Disk"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The disk Arch Linux is installed on. Everything on it is erased. The medium this runs from is not offered."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Storage"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK: what a wrong answer is told
#: module.yaml
msgid "Choose a disk that exists."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_ENCRYPTION_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Disk encryption"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_ENCRYPTION_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Encrypts the system, so the disk cannot be read without its password. That is yours unless it has one of its own, and it is asked at every boot."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK_PASSWORD_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Separate disk password"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK_PASSWORD_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "The disk asks for a password of its own, and the login screen for yours. For a machine several people share."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK_PASSWORD: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Disk password"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_DISK_PASSWORD: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Unlocks the disk at every boot. Asked right before the installation and never written to a file."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Secure Boot"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Signs the kernel and boot loader with keys of this machine. In setup mode the keys are enrolled for you; turn Secure Boot on afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "Boot"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_RECOVERY_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Repairs a system that no longer starts, without a USB stick: on a partition of its own, in the boot menu behind the space key."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_BOOTSPLASH_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Boot splash"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_BOOTSPLASH_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Shows a logo while the system starts instead of a wall of text."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_KERNEL_ARGS: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Kernel parameters"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_KERNEL_ARGS: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Extra kernel parameters, separated by spaces. Leave empty unless you need one."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_CORE_TWEAKS_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Core tweaks"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_CORE_TWEAKS_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Parallel downloads, a quiet boot, password feedback and tuned memory, disk and log settings. Nothing extra is installed."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_CORE_TWEAKS_ENABLED: the heading its row sits under
#: module.yaml
msgid "System"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_MULTILIB_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "32-bit support"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_MULTILIB_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Needed by Steam, Wine and other software that is still 32-bit."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_AUR_HELPER_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "AUR helper"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_AUR_HELPER_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "paru, for software from the Arch User Repository. Built on this machine, which takes about a quarter of an hour."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_CONTAINER_ENGINE: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Container engine"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_CONTAINER_ENGINE: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "docker runs a daemon as root, which most documentation assumes. podman runs none and answers to the docker command. Both bring compose."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_FIREWALL_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Firewall"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_FIREWALL_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Blocks incoming connections but SSH and printer discovery. A network marked home also reaches file sharing: nmcli connection modify <name> connection.zone home"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SSH_SERVER_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "SSH server"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SSH_SERVER_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Log in to this machine from another one with your account. Not as root."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_HOUSEKEEPING_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Housekeeping"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_HOUSEKEEPING_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Timers that rank the mirrors weekly, trim the package cache and check disk health."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_EDITOR: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Text editor"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_EDITOR: what it means
#: module.yaml
msgid "Opens wherever a command asks for an editor: sudoedit, git, systemctl edit. nano and micro type straight away; vim, neovim and helix are modal."
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SHELL_ENHANCEMENT_ENABLED: the question
#: module.yaml
msgid "Shell enhancement"
msgstr ""

#. ARCH_OS_SHELL_ENHANCEMENT_ENABLED: what it means
#: module.yaml
